<title>JAPAN: Japan April construction orders down 16.1% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan April construction orders down 16.1% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Orders received by 50 major Japanese construction companies fell 16.1 percent in April from a year earlier to 1.00 trillion yen, the Construction Ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>In March, orders rose 6.5 percent year-on-year to 3.33 trillion yen.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of overall construction orders in April (in yen, with year-ago percentage comparisons, all figures rounded):  Domestic private-sector orders   663.91 bln   -16.5 pct</p>
<p> Domestic public-sector orders    206.90 bln   -20.2 pct</p>
<p>Orders for foreign government facilities in Japan and orders   worth less than 10 million yen	 41.85 bln    -2.8 pct</p>
<p> Orders received abroad		90.54 bln    -7.8 pct</p>
</text>
